  "summary": "Beam-pruned dynamic programming now yields linear-time RNA accessibility, opening energy, and pseudoknot ensemble outputs from the same algorithmic framework.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread across these preprints is algorithmic scaling for RNA secondary structure analysis. LinearRaccess computes accessibility and opening energy deterministically in O(N) time via beam-pruned inside-outside dynamic programming, without base-pair span limits. LinearKnot applies beam pruning to approximate CParty's hierarchical density-2 pseudoknot ensembles, yielding linear-time partition functions, MFE, and loop probabilities. Both trade exactness for linear time through approximation. Spearfish addresses a different tooling problem, Δ-mapping of long reads to redundant transcriptomes, reported at 26-83x the speed of minimap2 with lower memory. A separate regulatory-genomics preprint reports that long-range information between vertebrates stops transferring before local sequence information does. The new element is the shared use of beam pruning to reach linear complexity in RNA ensemble calculations.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-12"
}
